# Build context filter for backend/Dockerfile's `COPY . .`.
#
# Without this file the whole backend/ tree is baked into the shipped
# image, which is a real problem on three counts:
#
#   1. Secrets. A developer's gitignored `backend/.env` (per the root
#      CLAUDE.md, the local override that wins over .env.development)
#      would be copied into a layer and shipped to ECS / the pilot VM.
#      Layers are not secrets storage — anyone who can pull the image
#      can read it.
#   2. A second, unmanaged Python install. `backend/.venv` is the dev's
#      local venv; it lands at /app/.venv with its own pip/setuptools on
#      whatever versions that laptop happened to have. Trivy scans it and
#      reports CVEs for packages the image doesn't actually run, and the
#      hash-pinned requirements.lock install stops being the whole story.
#   3. Size. The venv plus the tool caches are hundreds of MB of layer
#      for files nothing at runtime opens.
#
# Everything the running container needs stays: app/, alembic/,
# alembic.ini, main.py, pyproject.toml, requirements.lock, and scripts/
# (deploy/deploy.sh runs migrate_all_tenants.py and deploy/add-tenant.sh
# runs create_tenant.py inside this image).

# --- secrets: never in a layer ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.development
*.sops

# --- local virtualenvs / installed-package metadata ---
.venv
venv
*.egg-info

# --- tool + build caches ---
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.coverage
htmlcov

# --- not needed at runtime ---
tests
docs
.github
CLAUDE.md
README.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
requirements-dev.in
requirements-dev.lock

# --- service fixtures for the local compose stack only ---
authentik
keycloak
localstack
init-tenants.sql

# --- vcs / editor noise ---
.git
.gitignore
.DS_Store
